with human review.

11
00:00:27,838 --> 00:00:30,230
Watch us connect a KiCad circuit board, a

12
00:00:30,162 --> 00:00:33,918
FreeCAD enclosure, controller code and a working local

13
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,530
MQTT demonstration.

14
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:39,720
The schematic uses exactly four integrated circuits.

15
00:00:40,433 --> 00:00:43,160
Two seventy-four H C T one sixty-four shift

16
00:00:43,096 --> 00:00:44,565
registers receive the message.

17
00:00:45,278 --> 00:00:47,342
A six eighty-eight compares the address.

18
00:00:48,055 --> 00:00:50,553
A two seventy-three output register stores the LED

19
00:00:50,489 --> 00:00:50,976
pattern.

20
00:00:51,689 --> 00:00:53,890
Shifting and output storage are separate, so the

21
00:00:53,826 --> 00:00:55,741
lights do not change while the next message

22
00:00:55,678 --> 00:00:56,324
arrives.

23
00:00:57,233 --> 00:00:59,354
Why only eight LEDs for four chips?

24
00:01:00,067 --> 00:01:02,360
Two chips receive the sixteen serial bits.

25
00:01:03,073 --> 00:01:05,719
One compares the selected address, and one stores

26
00:01:05,656 --> 00:01:06,679
eight output bits.

27
00:01:07,393 --> 00:01:08,931
They perform different jobs.

28
00:01:09,644 --> 00:01:11,639
They are not four eight-channel LED drivers.

29
00:01:12,352 --> 00:01:15,204
A seventy-four H C five ninety-five combines shifting

30
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:17,970
and output storage, and could simplify another design.

31
00:01:18,683 --> 00:01:21,970
This version deliberately makes address reception, comparison and

32
00:01:21,906 --> 00:01:22,884
storage visible.

33
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:26,149
Four removable jumpers have the weights one, two,

34
00:01:26,337 --> 00:01:27,167
four and eight.

35
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,715
Add the fitted jumper values to choose an

36
00:01:29,651 --> 00:01:31,349
address from zero to fifteen.

37
00:01:32,062 --> 00:01:34,023
One plus four selects board five.

38
00:01:34,736 --> 00:01:37,440
Eight current-limited LEDs show the stored output byte.

39
00:01:38,333 --> 00:01:40,363
The controller sends an address byte, then an

40
00:01:40,299 --> 00:01:42,557
output byte, most significant bit first.

41
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:44,911
Keep strobe high while shifting.

42
00:01:45,624 --> 00:01:48,225
After the data settles, pulse strobe low, then

43
00:01:48,161 --> 00:01:48,671
high.

44
00:01:49,384 --> 00:01:51,562
Only the matching board stores the new pattern.

45
00:01:52,275 --> 00:01:54,499
The other boards keep their previous values.

46
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,064
Now the real PCB editor.

47
00:01:57,777 --> 00:01:59,898
This is a two-layer, one hundred and ten

48
00:01:59,834 --> 00:02:02,686
by eighty millimetre prototype, with through-hole parts and

49
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:03,898
four mounting holes.

50
00:02:04,611 --> 00:02:06,023
The project stays editable.

51
00:02:06,933 --> 00:02:08,414
First, front copper.

52
00:02:09,127 --> 00:02:11,157
The red tracks connect component pins on the

53
00:02:11,093 --> 00:02:11,843
top side.

54
00:02:12,556 --> 00:02:14,791
Vias allow a connection to move between the

55
00:02:14,727 --> 00:02:16,654
two copper layers.

56
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:18,825
These are actual KiCad layer changes recorded with

57
00:02:18,761 --> 00:02:19,488
OBS.

58
00:02:20,367 --> 00:02:21,676
Next, back copper.

59
00:02:22,389 --> 00:02:24,099
The blue tracks complete the routing.

60
00:02:24,812 --> 00:02:27,676
A ground-filled zone occupies the available space, with

61
00:02:27,612 --> 00:02:29,196
clearances around other nets.

62
00:02:29,909 --> 00:02:32,692
Short routes and local supply bypass capacitors matter,

63
00:02:32,857 --> 00:02:34,452
even on a slow logic board.

64
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:37,910
Silkscreen is the printed information for assembly and

65
00:02:37,846 --> 00:02:38,390
use.

66
00:02:39,104 --> 00:02:42,196
Here we identify the chip functions, jumper weights

67
00:02:42,132 --> 00:02:44,138
and LED numbers.

68
00:02:44,075 --> 00:02:46,138
Designed with OpenAI Codex is also printed on

69
00:02:46,074 --> 00:02:46,653
the board.

70
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:50,019
Solder mask is a separate manufacturing layer.

71
00:02:50,732 --> 00:02:52,899
Its openings expose the pads where solder must

72
00:02:52,835 --> 00:02:54,339
bond.

73
00:02:54,275 --> 00:02:56,590
It is not another copper layer.

74
00:02:56,526 --> 00:02:59,013
KiCad keeps these definitions separate from the electrical

75
00:02:58,949 --> 00:02:59,721
connections.

76
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,858
Edge Cuts defines the finished board outline.

77
00:03:03,571 --> 00:03:06,435
The drill exports separately describe plated connections and

78
00:03:06,371 --> 00:03:07,863
non-plated mounting holes.

79
00:03:08,576 --> 00:03:11,212
Mechanical dimensions must also agree with the future

80
00:03:11,148 --> 00:03:11,829
enclosure.

81
00:03:12,733 --> 00:03:14,923
The native KiCad board check reports zero design-rule

82
00:03:14,859 --> 00:03:18,694
violations, zero unconnected pads and zero footprint errors.

83
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:23,036
An ideal logic model passes sixty-five thousand, five

84
00:03:22,973 --> 00:03:25,825
hundred and thirty-six address and data combinations.

85
00:03:26,538 --> 00:03:29,264
Electrical rule checking, a physical build and bench

86
00:03:29,201 --> 00:03:30,419
testing still remain.

87
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:33,020
Now the components are on the board in

88
00:03:32,956 --> 00:03:36,974
three dimensions: four logic chips, eight red LEDs,

89
00:03:37,127 --> 00:03:40,814
resistors, bypass capacitors, the reset switch and headers.

90
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:43,419
This assembly comes from KiCad using its installed

91
00:03:43,355 --> 00:03:45,773
component models, exported as STEP and displayed in

92
00:03:45,709 --> 00:03:46,185
FreeCAD.

93
00:03:46,898 --> 00:03:49,419
STEP carries the component geometry here, but not

94
00:03:49,355 --> 00:03:51,704
the copper or silkscreen.

95
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:54,287
The earlier KiCad views show those manufacturing layers

96
00:03:54,223 --> 00:03:54,801
separately.

97
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:58,049
For the controller compartment, start with the official

98
00:03:57,986 --> 00:04:00,141
Espressif DevKit C version four drawing.

99
00:04:00,854 --> 00:04:03,260
The PCB is twenty-seven point nine four by

100
00:04:03,197 --> 00:04:05,260
forty-eight point two six millimetres.

101
00:04:05,973 --> 00:04:08,609
The module antenna extends beyond that board outline.

102
00:04:09,322 --> 00:04:11,945
Our reference includes that extension, so the plastic

103
00:04:11,882 --> 00:04:13,202
bay does not cut through it.

104
00:04:13,916 --> 00:04:16,825
Connector heights and cable space remain simplified estimates,

105
00:04:16,933 --> 00:04:18,745
to be checked against the actual board.

106
00:04:19,633 --> 00:04:21,857
In FreeCAD, the outside box is one hundred

107
00:04:21,793 --> 00:04:23,800
and ninety by one hundred and fifteen millimetres,

108
00:04:23,736 --> 00:04:25,891
with a thirty-four millimetre base height.

109
00:04:25,827 --> 00:04:28,634
Subtract an inner box to create a hollow

110
00:04:28,570 --> 00:04:28,954
shell.

111
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:31,753
The wall and floor are two point four

112
00:04:31,689 --> 00:04:32,439
millimetres.

113
00:04:33,152 --> 00:04:35,810
A dimension spreadsheet controls the main envelope and

114
00:04:35,746 --> 00:04:36,907
LED aperture size.

115
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:40,678
The feature tree retains the boxes, cylinders, unions

116
00:04:40,683 --> 00:04:42,004
and cuts used to build it.

117
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:46,244
Place four PCB supports at the actual mounting-hole

118
00:04:46,957 --> 00:04:47,306
positions.

119
00:04:47,242 --> 00:04:49,992
Check nearby components and solder leads, rather than

120
00:04:49,928 --> 00:04:53,409
assuming every screw hole has unlimited space around

121
00:04:53,345 --> 00:04:53,843
it.

122
00:04:53,779 --> 00:04:56,117
One original support touched a switch lead, so

123
00:04:56,053 --> 00:04:58,220
its diameter was reduced.

124
00:04:58,156 --> 00:05:00,311
Add separate lid screw bosses and a low

125
00:05:00,247 --> 00:05:02,071
divider between the main board and the ESP32

126
00:05:02,007 --> 00:05:02,311
bay.

127
00:05:02,247 --> 00:05:06,151
The final modelled parts have no solid intersections.

128
00:05:07,067 --> 00:05:08,730
The lid has eight aligned apertures.

129
00:05:09,444 --> 00:05:11,747
Their centres come from the transformed LED models,

130
00:05:11,843 --> 00:05:13,507
rather than from an approximate image.

131
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:16,147
Because the chips and capacitors are taller than

132
00:05:16,083 --> 00:05:18,421
the LED lenses, illustrative light guides carry the

133
00:05:18,357 --> 00:05:19,301
light up to the lid.

134
00:05:20,014 --> 00:05:22,306
Their optical performance and retention are not yet

135
00:05:22,243 --> 00:05:22,764
tested.

136
00:05:23,477 --> 00:05:25,998
Watch the aperture parameter change, and then return

137
00:05:25,934 --> 00:05:28,375
to the exported three point four millimetre size.

138
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:31,399
Lift the lid and inspect the complete assembly.

139
00:05:32,112 --> 00:05:34,302
The main PCB sits on its posts, and

140
00:05:34,238 --> 00:05:36,176
a separate cradle supports the ESP32 reference.

141
00:05:36,112 --> 00:05:39,935
The USB cable opening faces the controller connector.

142
00:05:39,872 --> 00:05:43,238
The antenna extension stays in a plastic region

143
00:05:43,174 --> 00:05:44,701
away from the main PCB.

144
00:05:44,637 --> 00:05:48,015
This is a mechanical concept with checked model

145
00:05:47,951 --> 00:05:48,312
clearances.

146
00:05:48,248 --> 00:05:53,294
Printing tolerance, fasteners, cooling, radio performance and a

147
00:05:53,230 --> 00:05:55,786
real USB plug still need physical testing.

148
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:59,152
Three control signals still need power and a

149
00:05:59,088 --> 00:06:02,969
common ground, so the drawing shows five connections.

150
00:06:02,905 --> 00:06:05,369
GPIO twenty-three goes to DATA, eighteen to CLOCK,

151
00:06:05,305 --> 00:06:07,117
and nineteen to STROBE.

152
00:06:07,831 --> 00:06:09,643
Ground goes to J one pin two;

153
00:06:09,808 --> 00:06:12,968
regulated five volts goes to pin one.

154
00:06:12,904 --> 00:06:15,220
These H C T inputs are suitable for

155
00:06:15,156 --> 00:06:18,065
three point three volt push-pull logic.

156
00:06:18,001 --> 00:06:20,773
Use short local wiring.

157
00:06:20,709 --> 00:06:22,556
Choose one appropriate power arrangement;

158
00:06:22,492 --> 00:06:25,447
do not combine USB and external ESP32 power

159
00:06:25,383 --> 00:06:25,962
inputs.

160
00:06:26,867 --> 00:06:28,873
The website sends a command through its local

161
00:06:28,809 --> 00:06:30,405
server to a real MQTT client.

162
00:06:30,341 --> 00:06:33,261
The broker delivers that message to the simulated

163
00:06:33,198 --> 00:06:35,330
controller, which publishes an acknowledgement.

164
00:06:35,266 --> 00:06:38,621
Only then does the dashboard update the displayed

165
00:06:38,557 --> 00:06:39,044
outputs.

166
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:42,301
The drawing animates the named wire paths so

167
00:06:42,237 --> 00:06:43,409
you can follow the signal chain.

168
00:06:43,345 --> 00:06:45,855
That animation explains the connections;

169
00:06:45,791 --> 00:06:48,312
it is not a measurement of current flowing

170
00:06:48,248 --> 00:06:49,546
through a physical circuit.

171
00:06:50,433 --> 00:06:52,394
Open the local address shown on screen.

172
00:06:53,107 --> 00:06:55,297
Choose the board address and click the requested

173
00:06:55,233 --> 00:06:57,137
LED pattern.

174
00:06:57,073 --> 00:07:01,616
Alternating LEDs sends the byte eighty-five, hexadecimal fifty-five.

175
00:07:01,552 --> 00:07:05,296
All LEDs on sends two hundred and fifty-five.

176
00:07:05,232 --> 00:07:07,056
The live trace shows both the command topic

177
00:07:06,992 --> 00:07:09,673
and the acknowledgement topic, with a sequence number

178
00:07:10,386 --> 00:07:10,804
connecting them.

179
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:12,941
We can see the broker and two connected

180
00:07:12,877 --> 00:07:14,861
MQTT clients responding to the website.

181
00:07:15,767 --> 00:07:18,288
Now deliberately send all LEDs on to address

182
00:07:18,224 --> 00:07:20,379
six while the board jumpers select five.

183
00:07:21,092 --> 00:07:23,636
The requested buttons change, but the stored output

184
00:07:23,572 --> 00:07:25,567
stays at hexadecimal fifty-five.

185
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,481
The acknowledgement reports an address mismatch.

186
00:07:29,194 --> 00:07:31,475
Return to address five and send again: now

187
00:07:31,411 --> 00:07:33,086
all eight indicators change.

188
00:07:33,799 --> 00:07:36,217
This demonstrates the reason for the address comparator

189
00:07:36,154 --> 00:07:37,737
and the separate output register.

190
00:07:38,451 --> 00:07:40,800
An unrelated command must not replace the stored

191
00:07:40,736 --> 00:07:41,211
pattern.

192
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:44,358
The demonstration is supplied with a start file,

193
00:07:44,466 --> 00:07:46,689
a pinned package lock and local source files.

194
00:07:47,402 --> 00:07:50,083
With a supported Node installation, run Start Demo.

195
00:07:50,796 --> 00:07:52,689
It installs the pinned dependencies if they are

196
00:07:52,625 --> 00:07:55,089
missing, then starts the web server and isolated

197
00:07:55,025 --> 00:07:55,534
broker.

198
00:07:56,247 --> 00:07:58,014
Both listen only on this computer.

199
00:07:58,727 --> 00:08:00,631
Close the running command window or stop the

200
00:08:00,567 --> 00:08:01,808
process to end the demo.

201
00:08:02,521 --> 00:08:04,699
The setup does not change an existing server

202
00:08:04,635 --> 00:08:05,773
or production broker.

203
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:09,552
The controller example separates Wi-Fi and MQTT handling

204
00:08:09,488 --> 00:08:11,049
from the sixteen-bit output routine.

205
00:08:10,985 --> 00:08:14,843
It starts STROBE high, shifts the address and

206
00:08:14,779 --> 00:08:17,289
LED bytes most significant bit first, waits for

207
00:08:17,225 --> 00:08:20,603
settling, then pulses STROBE low and high.

208
00:08:20,539 --> 00:08:23,414
No clock edge occurs during that low pulse.

209
00:08:23,350 --> 00:08:26,511
The example uses placeholders for network credentials and

210
00:08:26,447 --> 00:08:28,636
a separate configured broker.

211
00:08:28,573 --> 00:08:30,225
It has not been flashed or tested on

212
00:08:30,161 --> 00:08:32,053
an ESP32 in this demonstration.

213
00:08:32,933 --> 00:08:35,294
One two seven point zero point zero point

214
00:08:35,230 --> 00:08:38,277
one always means the device you are using.

215
00:08:38,213 --> 00:08:40,505
A physical ESP32 cannot reach this computer by

216
00:08:40,441 --> 00:08:42,151
connecting to its own loopback address.

217
00:08:42,087 --> 00:08:45,351
A later hardware test needs an accessible broker

218
00:08:45,287 --> 00:08:49,762
address, authentication, restricted topics and appropriate network protection.

219
00:08:49,698 --> 00:08:53,213
The supplied local demo intentionally stays isolated.

220
00:08:53,149 --> 00:08:56,755
The logic simulation and geometry checks are useful

221
00:08:56,691 --> 00:08:59,464
evidence, but they do not replace electrical rule

222
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,732
checking or bench testing.

223
00:09:01,633 --> 00:09:04,166
The Gerber layers and drill files are bundled

224
00:09:04,879 --> 00:09:05,251
together.

225
00:09:05,187 --> 00:09:09,045
After reviewing the fabrication preview and selected manufacturing

226
00:09:08,981 --> 00:09:10,999
options, these files can be uploaded to PCBWay

227
00:09:10,935 --> 00:09:11,376
for production.

228
00:09:11,313 --> 00:09:14,896
No manufacturing order has been placed.

229
